# UDS Bench example: error cases. Each block shows a problem the decoder flags.
# Formats are mixed on purpose: candump -L, plain "ID: bytes", Vector ASC and raw payloads.

# 1. Security: a wrong key is rejected with negative response 0x35 invalidKey.
(0.000000) can0 7E0#021003AAAAAAAAAA
(0.002000) can0 7E8#065003003201F4AA
(0.100000) can0 7E0#022701AAAAAAAAAA
(0.102000) can0 7E8#06670112345678AA
(0.200000) can0 7E0#06270200000000AA
(0.202000) can0 7E8#037F2735AAAAAAAA

# 2. Unknown DID: negative response 0x31 requestOutOfRange.
7E0: 03 22 DE AD AA AA AA AA
7E8: 03 7F 22 31 AA AA AA AA

# 3. Sequence error: SN 3 arrives where SN 1 is expected; the next CF is then an orphan.
(0.400000) can0 7E0#0322F190AAAAAAAA
(0.402000) can0 7E8#101462F190454754
(0.403000) can0 7E0#300000AAAAAAAAAA
(0.403200) can0 7E8#2345535431323334
(0.403400) can0 7E8#2235363738393031

# 4. The tester answers a First Frame with Overflow; the response stays incomplete.
(0.500000) can0 7E0#031902FFAAAAAAAA
(0.502000) can0 7E8#100F5902FF030000
(0.503000) can0 7E0#320000AAAAAAAAAA

# 5. Vector ASC lines: an invalid PCI type, then SF_DL 0 in a classic frame.
   0.600000 1  7E8             Rx   d 8 41 12 34 56 78 00 00 00
   0.700000 1  7E0             Tx   d 8 00 10 03 00 00 00 00 00

# 6. Raw payloads: a truncated request and an unknown service. Then a malformed line (odd digit count).
10
55 01 02
7E0#021003000000000
